  "result": "I added `top_words(text, n)` for issue #12 and opened a PR for it: https://github.com/acme/textstats/pull/7. All 9 tests pass, including 6 new ones for `top_words`.\n\n**What it does** (in `textstats/__init__.py`):\n- Returns up to `n` `(word, count)` pairs, most frequent first.\n- Ignores case, and reports every word in lowercase.\n- Ignores punctuation, so `hello,` and `hello!` both count as `hello`.\n- Breaks ties alphabetically.\n- Returns `[]` for empty text.\n- Uses only the standard library, as the reviewer asked.\n\n**Two choices the issue didn't cover:**\n- Apostrophes inside a word are kept, so `don't` counts as one word rather than becoming `dont` or `don` + `t`.\n- If `n` is 0 or negative, it returns `[]`.\n\n**Tests:** the new tests in `tests/test_textstats.py` cover each point in the issue's acceptance criteria, plus the two choices above.\n\nThe work is committed on a new branch, `issue-12-top-words`, and the commit message includes \"Closes #12\", so merging the PR will close the issue.",
